# Secrets must never enter the build context.
#
# Nothing copies them today — every COPY in the Dockerfiles names a specific path — so this is a
# guard against the ordinary future edit, a `COPY . .` or a new `COPY packages/x packages/x` that
# sweeps up a sibling `.env`. A secret baked into an image layer stays in that layer even if a
# later step deletes it, and the image gets pushed to a registry.
#
# `.env` and `deploy/.env` are the symlinks setup.sh creates so compose resolves ${VAR}; .env.docker
# is the one real file, holding JWT_SECRET, PII_ENCRYPTION_KEY and both database and MinIO passwords.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.production.example
